    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** (82.40) serving as the offensive engine. His matchup against Cavalli offers an ideal intersection of elite hitting environment and order-driven volume, making him our highest-ceiling asset. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also projects as a high-tier start; his rating is bolstered significantly by a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Bassitt, while **Heliot Ramos** (66.96) remains a high-value play despite the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, as he benefits from a strong park factor and a favorable matchup against the hittable Luis Severino. Conversely, **Jackson Merrill** (52.65) faces the toughest test of the day against Gilbert, whose elite xERA of 2.98 suppressed an otherwise strong base projection.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (44.92), who fell just shy of the threshold to displace **Miguel Vargas** or **Andy Pages**. While **Coby Mayo** maintains a respectable profile, his lower projected batting order spot and negative platoon weighting against Cavalli tipped the scales in favor of keeping him sidelined to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (59.41) continues to provide efficient utility production, with his elite xwOBA of 0.402 offsetting a neutral park factor against Taillon.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding our limited depth as we wait for the eventual returns of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Kyle Tucker** to the active roster. We are currently navigating a thin bench, with **Nolan Schanuel** providing emergency coverage if late-breaking lineup changes occur. Today\u2019s success hinges on our top-order catalysts\u2014**Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014capitalizing on their respective matchups to manufacture the stolen bases and run production required to stay competitive in our league\u2019s tight 5x5 race.",
